          "final_text_tail": " `llama-index-core/llama_index/core/base/llms/types.py` (the only file both PRs target):\n\n**Task 1 \u2014 Lazy mimetype accessor** (`types.py:87`):\n- New `ImageBlock.get_image_mimetype()` method: returns the cached `image_mimetype` if set; otherwise guesses via `filetype.guess` on the image data, caches the result in `image_mimetype`, and returns it (`None` if undeterminable).\n- `image_to_base64` now delegates to `self.get_image_mimetype()` instead of inlining the guess logic (`types.py:80`).\n\n**Task 2 \u2014 `encoding` field** (`types.py:58`):\n- New field `encoding: Literal[\"base64\", \"raw\"] = \"base64\"`.\n- `image_to_base64` only base64-encodes when `encoding == \"base64\"`; with `encoding=\"raw\"` the image bytes are kept as-is (`types.py:82-83`). Default preserves existing behavior; invalid values are rejected by pydantic.\n\nVerification:\n- All 12 existing tests in `tests/base/llms/test_types.py` pass.\n- Functional checks passed: lazy guess + caching, preset mimetype returned without guessing, `None` for image-less blocks, default base64 behavior unchanged, `raw` keeps raw bytes (mimetype still resolved), invalid `encoding` raises, `model_dump` includes `encoding`.\n- One pre-existing, unrelated failure in `tests/llms/test_callbacks.py` confirmed to fail on the unmodified code as well.\n\nNote: to run the tests I had to cache NLTK data (stopwords, punkt_tab) into the repo's gitignored `nltk_cache` dir after relaxing its group-write bit, since `llama_index.core` imports trigger NLTK downloads.",
